# Project Structure Guide

This document outlines the directory structure and important files in the sf-isv-cursor-rules project.

## Root Directory Structure

```
sf-isv-cursor-rules/
├── .cursor/                    # Cursor IDE configuration
│   └── rules/                 # Cursor rules and configurations
│       ├── agent-scratch-def.json
│       ├── cursor-rules.mdc
│       └── project-structure.mdc
├── config/                    # Project configuration files
│   └── project-scratch-def.json
├── force-app/                 # Salesforce metadata (main source)
│   └── main/
│       └── default/           # Default namespace metadata
│           ├── applications/  # Custom applications
│           ├── aura/          # Aura components
│           ├── classes/       # Apex classes
│           ├── contentassets/ # Content assets
│           ├── flexipages/    # Lightning pages
│           ├── layouts/       # Page layouts
│           ├── lwc/           # Lightning Web Components
│           ├── objects/       # Custom objects
│           ├── permissionsets/ # Permission sets
│           ├── staticresources/ # Static resources
│           ├── tabs/          # Custom tabs
│           └── triggers/      # Apex triggers
├── scripts/                   # Development scripts
│   ├── apex/                  # Apex code snippets
│   │   └── hello.apex
│   └── soql/                  # SOQL query examples
│       └── account.soql
├── jest.config.js             # Jest testing configuration
├── LICENSE                    # Project license
├── package.json               # Node.js dependencies
├── README.md                  # Project documentation
└── sfdx-project.json         # Salesforce DX project configuration
```

## Important Files and Directories

### Configuration Files
- **`sfdx-project.json`**: Salesforce DX project configuration defining the project structure and metadata
- **`package.json`**: Node.js dependencies and scripts for the project
- **`jest.config.js`**: Jest testing framework configuration
- **`config/project-scratch-def.json`**: Scratch org definition for development

### Cursor IDE Files
- **`.cursor/rules/`**: Contains all Cursor rules and IDE configurations
  - `cursor-rules.mdc`: Guidelines for adding/editing Cursor rules
  - `agent-scratch-def.json`: Agent-specific scratch org configuration
  - `project-structure.mdc`: This file documenting project structure

### Salesforce Metadata
- **`force-app/main/default/`**: Main source directory for Salesforce metadata
  - **`classes/`**: Apex classes (currently empty)
  - **`lwc/`**: Lightning Web Components (currently empty)
  - **`objects/`**: Custom objects and fields (currently empty)
  - **`triggers/`**: Apex triggers (currently empty)
  - **`applications/`**: Custom applications
  - **`aura/`**: Aura components
  - **`permissionsets/`**: Permission sets
  - **`staticresources/`**: Static resources (images, CSS, JS)
  - **`tabs/`**: Custom tabs
  - **`layouts/`**: Page layouts
  - **`flexipages/`**: Lightning pages
  - **`contentassets/`**: Content assets

### Development Scripts
- **`scripts/apex/`**: Contains Apex code snippets and examples
- **`scripts/soql/`**: Contains SOQL query examples

## Development Guidelines

1. **Salesforce Metadata**: Place all Salesforce metadata in `force-app/main/default/` following the standard Salesforce DX structure
2. **Cursor Rules**: Add new Cursor rules in `.cursor/rules/` with `.mdc` extension
3. **Scripts**: Development and testing scripts go in the `scripts/` directory
4. **Configuration**: Project-wide configuration files go in the `config/` directory

## File Naming Conventions

- Use kebab-case for directory names
- Use PascalCase for Salesforce metadata (classes, components, etc.)
- Use camelCase for JavaScript/TypeScript files
- Use descriptive names that clearly indicate purpose